data: {"level":2,"reviewed":{"level":2,"label":"formula / approach","text":"Let $m = \\max_k z_k$ taken along `axis`. Then $\\operatorname{softmax}(\\mathbf{z}) = e^{\\mathbf{z}-m} / \\sum_k e^{z_k - m}$,\nand every exponent $z_k - m$ is at most $0$. Check that the same identity holds for each slice of a\nmatrix, and that the maximum you subtract belongs to the slice you are normalising."},"hints_note":null}

